{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Tripoli a noble family of the Kingdom of Jerusalem. He was the son of Pons of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Born around 1130 he was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187.\n\n* **Family and Succession** * \nRaymond III was the son of Pons of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He had at least one brother named Bohemond III who succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. Raymond III married Eschiva of Bures and they had several children including Bohemond IV and Alice of Tripoli. \n\n* **Conflict with the Ayyubid Sultan** *\nIn 1163 Raymond III allied with the Byzantine Empire against the Fatimid Caliphate. However in 1164 he switched sides and allied with the Fatimids against the Byzantines. This change of allegiance was motivated by the promise of the Fatimid Caliph of giving him control over the County of Sidon. The Fatimid Caliph however failed to deliver on this promise and Raymond III allied with the Crusaders and the Byzantines again. In 1171 he allied with the Crusaders and the Byzantines to take the County of Sidon from the Fatimid Caliph.\n\n* **Second Crusade** *\nIn 1187 Raymond III joined the Second Crusade led by King Guy of Jerusalem. However he did not participate in the actual fighting and instead remained in Tripoli to defend it against the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin. \n\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the Second Crusade. He was succeeded by his son Bohemond IV who became the Count of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.02614368}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.0001275458}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.001016934}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1430125}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -9.250213e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0001643761}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -4.5894525e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.019333376}, {"token"